From: oplus-sukisu_kernel maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] lsm_count: reserve a static-call slot for builtin CONFIG_KSU

Linux 6.12 sizes lsm_idlist[] and static_calls_table[] at compile time via
MAX_LSM_COUNT in include/linux/lsm_count.h, counting only the 14 mainline LSM
Kconfig symbols. On stock android16-6.12 gki_defconfig (CAPABILITIES, SELINUX,
SAFESETID, BPF_LSM, LANDLOCK), MAX_LSM_COUNT evaluates to 5 and all 5 slots are
taken during security_init().

When SukiSU-Ultra builtin runs ksu_lsm_hook_init() from device_initcall() and
calls security_add_hooks(..., &ksu_lsm_id), security_add_hooks() sees
lsm_active_cnt >= MAX_LSM_COUNT (5 >= 5) and panics before userspace starts.

Account for CONFIG_KSU in MAX_LSM_COUNT so SukiSU gets its own slot.

diff --git a/include/linux/lsm_count.h b/include/linux/lsm_count.h
--- a/include/linux/lsm_count.h
+++ b/include/linux/lsm_count.h
@@ -100,6 +100,12 @@
 #define IPE_ENABLED
 #endif
 
+#if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_KSU)
+#define KSU_LSM_ENABLED 1,
+#else
+#define KSU_LSM_ENABLED
+#endif
+
 /*
  *  There is a trailing comma that we need to be accounted for. This is done by
  *  using a skipped argument in __COUNT_LSMS
@@ -122,7 +128,8 @@
 		LANDLOCK_ENABLED	\
 		IMA_ENABLED		\
 		EVM_ENABLED		\
-		IPE_ENABLED)
+		IPE_ENABLED		\
+		KSU_LSM_ENABLED)
 
 #else
 
